specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:163:### 4.3 list_sessions
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:165:Requests the authenticated user's conversation summaries. The frame may omit paging fields; when present, `limit` is a non-negative integer and `before` is a cursor with a 1–128 character `sessionId` and a finite date in `updatedAt`. Unknown fields, including a client-supplied user id, are ignored ([validated by: accepts list_sessions and rejects malformed paging fields](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L25)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:169:| `type`   | string | Yes      | `"list_sessions"`              |
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:300:- An entry **opened while suppression is already active** is announced with `entry_skip` and nothing else: no `entry_upsert`, no `entry_delta`, no `entry_commit` follows it ([validated by: skips rather than upserts a segment opened after suppression](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L314)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:349:- Any other failure raised while processing a message is reported as `SERVER_ERROR` ([validated by: reports any other failure as a server error](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L431)).
specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md:15:- Any other failure produces `error` (`SERVER_ERROR`) then `stream_end` ([validated by: reports any other failure as a server error](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L431)).
specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md:16:- A `user_message` that fails validation (empty, blank or over-length content) never reaches the orchestrator and still produces `error` (`INVALID_MESSAGE`) then `stream_end` ([validated by: answers an empty user_message with INVALID_MESSAGE then stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L465), [validated by: answers a blank user_message with INVALID_MESSAGE then stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L469), [validated by: answers an over-length user_message with INVALID_MESSAGE then stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L473)).
specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md:17:- A malformed `ping` produces `error` (`INVALID_MESSAGE`) and no `stream_end` ([validated by: answers a malformed ping with INVALID_MESSAGE and no stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L477)).
specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md:19:- A malformed `ping` arriving mid-run gets its own `error` frame, the run's deltas continue unaffected, and exactly one `stream_end` is the very last frame ([validated by: keeps one stream_end, last, when a malformed ping lands mid-run](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L485)).
specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md:26:- The client rule that a stream is complete at either `stream_end` or `error` is deleted with it: an `error` frame is advisory, and a run is complete at `stream_end` or when the socket closes ([validated by: keeps one stream_end, last, when a malformed ping lands mid-run](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L485)).
specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md:27:- No special case sending `stream_end` for a single error code existed to remove, because the general rule covers every code ([validated by: reports any other failure as a server error](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L431)).
specs/hal-engine-commit-open-entries/spec.md:14:- A thinking segment open when the provider throws is committed as well, so both open entries are covered, not only the assistant one ([validated by: commits an open thinking entry too when the provider throws mid-thought](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L546)).
specs/hal-engine-commit-open-entries/spec.md:16:- A turn that ends on `stop` sends exactly one `entry_commit` per opened entry: the `stop` path clears both open indices, so the `finally` after it commits nothing twice ([validated by: sends one commit per opened entry when the turn ends on a stop chunk](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L574)).
specs/hal-engine-commit-open-entries/spec.md:29:- A thinking entry cut off mid-thought is flagged the same way ([validated by: flags an open thinking entry truncated when the provider throws mid-thought](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L618)).
specs/hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md:78:- A client sends `{type: 'list_sessions', limit?, before?}` and receives `{type: 'session_list', sessions}` for the socket's authenticated user, with `createdAt` and `updatedAt` serialised as ISO-8601 strings and any client-supplied `userId` ignored ([validated by: answers list_sessions from the injected session store with ISO summaries](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L124), [validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L91)).
specs/hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md:79:- A store without `listFor` answers `{type: 'session_list', sessions: []}`, and a throwing `listFor` logs an error on the `ws` category and answers `{type: 'error', code: 'SERVER_ERROR'}` ([validated by: answers an empty session_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L132), [validated by: logs list_sessions failures on ws with the authenticated user and answers SERVER_ERROR](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L158)).
specs/hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md:80:- The validator accepts an optional non-negative integer `limit` and an optional `before` cursor whose `sessionId` is 1–128 characters and whose `updatedAt` parses as a valid timestamp, rejecting any other `list_sessions` payload with `INVALID_MESSAGE` without calling `listFor` ([validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame and rejects a malformed limit or before with INVALID_MESSAGE without calling listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L161)).
specs/hal-engine-session-resume/spec.md:31:- A segment opened after suppression, which the client was only ever sent as a skip, is marked `suppressed` too ([validated by: marks a segment opened after suppression as suppressed in the session](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L357)).
